Error: Jet.InvalidRegexLiteral: A `String` is not a `Regex` pattern
  --> Tests/UI/regex_bare_string.jet:4:27
    |
  4 | run: fn() { print(re.find("\\d+", "id=42") ?? "none") }
    |                           ^^^^^^
 Why: Regex patterns are typed literals, so Jet can validate them before the program runs
 Fix: Write `Regex{"..."}` here, or call `re.compile(text)` for a pattern built at run time
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.InvalidRegexLiteral
